# What must NOT go into the image.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, so `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile took the
# whole working directory. Three separate problems, worst first:
#
#   1. .env went in. That file holds the live Paddle API key, the SMTP
#      password, the Groq key and the settings encryption key. Anyone
#      who can pull the image can read them - `docker history` and an
#      unpacked layer are enough, and deleting the file in a later layer
#      does not remove it from the earlier one.
#   2. app.db went in, so a published image would carry real accounts,
#      real conversations and real email addresses.
#   3. .venv, node_modules and the brain checkpoints went in, which is
#      hundreds of megabytes of host-specific binaries that the image
#      cannot use anyway - it installs its own from
#      requirements-cloud.txt.
#
# Anything listed here is also excluded from the build CONTEXT, so it is
# never even uploaded to the daemon. That is why the build gets faster
# as well as smaller and safer.

# ---- secrets. Never, under any circumstances. ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
secrets/

# ---- real data ----
app.db
app.db-wal
app.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/
chat_data.json
credits.json
users.json
logs/

# ---- things the image builds for itself ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/dist/

# ---- large local artefacts the container never runs ----
# The local image and language models, and their caches. The container
# is CPU-only and answers from Groq - see the Dockerfile's note on why
# torch is not installed either.
brain/checkpoint-*.npz
brain/corpus/
.cache/
.ollama/
models/
mobile/
desktop/

# ---- user-generated content, regenerated at runtime ----
static/uploads/
static/generated/
static/video/renders/

# ---- version control and editor noise ----
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- local-only tooling that has no job inside the container ----
.claude/
tools/
scripts/
deploy/
deploy.sh
cloudflared-config.yml
*.md
!README.md
